INT. FLOODED RICE MILL - NIGHT

Knee-deep brown water. Sacks float like dead cattle. SERGEANT OKAFOR, 40s, scarred jaw, holds a lantern low. CORPORAL HALVORSEN, 20s, freckled, covers the door with a rifle. PRIVATE LIN, 19, thin, shivers beside a radio set.

A man in a farmer's coat wades out of the dark. Hands up. STRANGER, 50s, mud to the waist.

STRANGER
Don't shoot. I live here.

OKAFOR
Nobody lives here. Name.

STRANGER
Teodor. Teodor Vasko. The mill is my brother's.

Halvorsen steps closer. Lin keeps her eyes on the radio.

HALVORSEN
Sarge, he came from the north bank. That's their side.

TEODOR
The bridge is gone. I swam.

Distant engines. Okafor kills the lantern. Dark.

OKAFOR
(whispering)
Lin. Radio. Now.

LIN
Static, Sergeant. Only static.

The engines grow louder. Halvorsen cocks the rifle.
